ruby-data/index.json
====================

`index.json` is derived data distributed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), because it is
derived from sources under that licence.

It is generated by `cozyll data fetch` from the sources recorded in
`sources.yaml`. The default source set is:

- KANJIDIC — kanji grades and metadata.
  © Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group (EDRDG).
  CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project
  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html

- JMdict — word readings.
  © EDRDG. CC BY-SA 4.0
  https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project

- JMnedict — proper-name readings.
  © EDRDG. CC BY-SA 4.0
  https://www.edrdg.org/enamdict/enamdict_doc.html

- JmdictFurigana / JmnedictFurigana — kanji/reading alignments.
  © Doublevil. CC BY-SA 4.0
  https://github.com/Doublevil/JmdictFurigana

- yomitan-jlpt-vocab — JLPT vocabulary with JMdict entry IDs.
  CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://github.com/stephenmk/yomitan-jlpt-vocab

- Jonathan Waller's JLPT Resources — JLPT levels.
  © Jonathan Waller. CC BY — http://www.tanos.co.uk/jlpt/

- kanji-data — JSON conversion and JLPT data.
  MIT (scripts) — https://github.com/davidluzgouveia/kanji-data

Changes: the upstream files are reduced to the jōyō/JLPT kanji, word, and
segment tables and converted to the canonical `index.json` format. See
`sources.yaml` for the pinned revisions.

The upstream notices above continue to apply; this data must not be claimed as
the site author's copyright. Cozyll itself ships none of this data.
